     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is twice the usual FDA-labeled maximum:\n- Immediate-release: 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- Extended-release: 2,000 to 2,500 mg/day.\n\nAt this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you meant if 1700 was a typo.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg, depending on the patient's titration.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
